&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the Aviatrix Customer Enablement team to shape the next generation of our Aviatrix Certified Engineer (ACE) program. We&#39;re looking for a Senior Technical Instructional Designer to join our customer facing enablement team. You&#39;ll partner with deep technical SMEs (CCIE-level networking experts) and bring the instructional design muscle — designing self-paced, on-demand, and immersive learning experiences for enterprise practitioners. Near-term, you&#39;ll co-deliver live bootcamps; longer-term, you&#39;ll own the vision for how customers learn Aviatrix.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Position Responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-deliver multi-day ACE bootcamps and workshops alongside technical SMEs (near-term focus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect self-paced, on-demand learning paths and an immersive curriculum for cloud networking practitioners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce how-to videos, interactive labs, and practitioner reference documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-powered tools to accelerate content creation and scale the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design measurement frameworks to track learning outcomes and program effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring modern L&amp;amp;D best practices (adult learning, digital enablement) to a highly technical team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Requirements&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in instructional design, L&amp;amp;D, or technical training — with meaningful time in technical/IT subject matter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record building self-paced and on-demand learning programs (not only instructor-led)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools to create or enhance technical learning content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience producing professional video-based training (scripting, storyboarding, recording)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong live facilitation skills — comfortable co-delivering technical workshops for enterprise audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to partner with SMEs to distill complex topics into clear, structured curricula&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LMS administration, learning analytics, or certification program design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer education or external-facing enablement background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in the US (NAM region)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS Solutions Architect Associate (SAA-C03) or Azure Fundamentals — especially if paired with a track record of self-learning complex technical domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in networking, cloud, or cybersecurity training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TECHNICAL DOMAIN CONTEXT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t configure these technologies — you&#39;ll design learning around them. Conceptual familiarity with any of the following is a plus: multi-cloud networking (AWS VPC, Azure VNet), routing fundamentals (BGP, OSPF), SD-WAN, enterprise VPN, cloud security. Relevant certs in this space include CCIE, AWS ANS-C01, and Azure AZ-700. If you learn new technical domains quickly by working with experts, you&#39;ll thrive here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
