&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Aviatrix® is pioneering the Cloud Native Security Fabric — the architecture the Containment Era requires. The Cloud Native Security Fabric governs every workload communication path across every cloud, every VPC, every Kubernetes cluster, and every serverless function, from a single policy plane. One rule. Universal propagation. Enforced at the workload, not at a chokepoint. Trusted by more than 500 of the world&#39;s leading enterprises. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://aviatrix.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;aviatrix.ai&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role - Staff Engineer – Backend Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aviatrix Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) delivers the intelligence, network, and security services of Aviatrix&#39;s multi-cloud platform as a managed offering, built on modern microservices architecture. We&#39;re seeking a Staff Engineer for our SaaS Platform team to bring technical depth to backend engineering, contribute to distributed microservices and cloud-native infrastructure design on AWS, mentor junior engineers, and raise the bar on reliability, performance, and security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Technical Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design and delivery of backend platform features, breaking down complex projects into scoped tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architecture discussions on scalability, fault tolerance, multi-tenancy, and operational simplicity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on core platform services using AWS-managed services (Aurora, MSK/Kafka, ClickHouse)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate trade-offs on technology choices, system boundaries, and API contracts; write clear design docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Engineering Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design high-performance microservices using gRPC, REST, and event-driven patterns (Golang preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce best practices for observability, resiliency, and SLO-driven operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to supportability (runbooks, diagnostics) and apply security best practices across service boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews, capacity planning, and incident retrospectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior engineers through code reviews, design discussions, and 1-on-1s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Management; participate in on-call and incident RCA; support recruiting as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years software engineering experience, with some mentoring experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on a SaaS/PaaS product with high-availability, multi-tenancy exposure; comfortable with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend &amp;amp; Microservices&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Golang preferred; production-grade gRPC microservices experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grasp of distributed systems (consistency, fault tolerance, service discovery, circuit breaking, back-pressure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in data structures, algorithms, OS, and systems programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API design/versioning experience (REST and gRPC), backward compatibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SaaS Platform &amp;amp; AWS Managed Services&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-tenancy and high-availability design patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AWS-managed services (Aurora, MSK/Kafka, ClickHouse); event-driven systems (SQS, SNS) a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Deployment &amp;amp; Supportability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience deploying/operating production services, release management, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of observability, alerting, diagnostics, and runbooks; incident response and RCA experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AWS &amp;amp; Cloud Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS as primary cloud platform; familiarity with Kubernetes (EKS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with IaC (Terraform, CDK, CloudFormation) and CI/CD for cloud-native services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring/logging/tracing or platform-management tooling experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional AWS services (RDS, DynamoDB, Redshift, OpenSearch, Lambda); multi-cloud (Azure, GCP) exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network security, cloud networking, or SASE/SD-WAN background; open-source contributions or technical writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interpersonal &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written/verbal communication; effective in collaborative, distributed teams; skilled at mentoring and building consensus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
